-- title:
--   Finiteness of the two chart rings over R[X]
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian domain which is a unique factorisation monoid, let $K_0$ be a field which is a fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be a field equipped with compatible $R$- and $K_0$-algebra structures (so $R \to K_0 \to F$ is a tower). Let $j \in F$ be nonzero and transcendental over $R$, and assume that $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$ obtained by adjoining $j$ to $K_0$ inside $F$. Write $A_0 =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $A_\infty =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$. Regard each of these as an algebra over the polynomial ring $R[X]$ by means of the $R$-algebra maps sending $X$ to $j$, respectively to $j^{-1}$ (the maps `polynomialToChartFin` and `polynomialToChartInf`, given by evaluation at the distinguished elements $j \in A_0$ and $j^{-1} \in A_\infty$). The assertion is the conjunction: $A_0$ is a finite $R[X]$-module, and $A_\infty$ is a finite $R[X]$-module.
--
--   This is the finiteness of the integral closure of $R[j]$, respectively $R[1/j]$, in a finite separable extension $F$ of $K_0(j)$, and it is the basic finiteness property of the affine charts out of which the two-chart integral model of the curve is glued. It strengthens the corresponding finite-type statement, and is used throughout the analysis of those charts (localisation and unit properties at a branch datum, smoothness after base change in characteristic zero, and the description of prime divisors coming from valuation subrings).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_finite_polynomial_chartAlgFin_and_chartAlgInf.lean

